    "Proposal title": "How to Build Resilient Systems That Don't Fail",
    "Session type": { "en": "Keynote" },
    "Track": { "en": "AI platforms at scale" },
    "Tags": null,
    "Description": "We spent decades teaching software to be rigid, type-safe, and deterministic. Then, overnight, we gave probabilistic, hallucination-prone text generators access to corporate databases, credit cards, physical turnstiles, and code repositories.\n\nThis talk deconstructs the most spectacular, bizarre, and quiet AI disasters in the wild, from legal fiascos and supply chain slop squatting to automated physical lockouts.\n\nAttendees will walk away with a battle-tested architectural framework to safely sandbox autonomous agents before their bot signs a contract or downloads malware.",
